Author:     Fabricio Breve <fbreve@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Tue Oct 20 13:13:55 2026 -0300
Commit:     Fabricio Breve <fbreve@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Tue Oct 20 13:13:55 2026 -0300

    Preserve EEPROM state and contents across savestates
    
    Preserve the complete local 93C46 protocol state and 128-byte EEPROM backing store across savestate save/load cycles.
    
    Freeze EEPROM progress during savestate transport to keep protocol and memory state coherent, restore the backing store before protocol state, and refill the EEPROM read path before resuming execution.
    
    Extend the tagged savestate format to version 4 with additional protocol state and a dedicated EEPROM memory payload. Legacy snapshots remain supported, retain their current backing contents, and deterministically normalize protocol state that was not previously stored.
    
    Add protocol replay, backing-store, DDRAM stall, persistence, and legacy compatibility coverage.

